<!--
  edet's mark, as a notification icon.

  **A status-bar icon cannot be the launcher icon**, and this is the whole
  reason this file exists rather than a `setSmallIcon(applicationInfo.icon)`.
  Android masks a small icon to its ALPHA and tints the result: an adaptive
  launcher icon, whose square is opaque edge to edge, renders as a solid white
  block. So the mark is redrawn here as the silhouette the platform can show —
  the same mesh geometry as `icon.svg`, in white on transparent — and the
  coloured icon goes on the notification's LARGE icon, where it is drawn as it
  is (`AcceptanceService.build`).

  One stroke width for every edge, where the source varies them between 2.8 and
  4.3: this is rendered at 24dp, where that difference is below a pixel.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="100"
    android:viewportHeight="100">
